+Reading from a file
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+Use :func:`~rich.progress.open` to read a file while a progress bar shows how many bytes have been read. The default mode is text, as with the built-in ``open``. The default total is the size of the file in bytes, so the bar fills as the file is read::
+
+    import json
+    from rich.progress import open
+
+    with open("data.json") as file:
+        data = json.load(file)
+
+Use mode ``"rb"`` to read bytes instead of text::
+
+    from rich.progress import open
+
+    with open("data.bin", "rb") as file:
+        data = file.read()
+
+To add a file to a progress display you already manage, use :meth:`~rich.progress.Progress.open` on a :class:`~rich.progress.Progress` instance. It does not start the display, so start it with a ``with`` block. Pass ``task_id`` to advance an existing task, or ``description`` to name a new one::
+
+    from rich.progress import Progress
+
+    progress = Progress()
+    with progress:
+        with progress.open("data.json", mode="rb", description="Loading") as file:
+            data = file.read()
+
+Reading from a file-like object
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+Use :func:`~rich.progress.wrap_file` to track reads from a binary file-like object that you have already opened. The reader is binary only. Pass ``total``, the size of the file in bytes, because it cannot be read from a file-like object. The reader does not close the file you passed in, so that file stays open after the ``with`` block::
+
+    import os
+    from rich.progress import wrap_file
+
+    size = os.path.getsize("data.bin")
+    with open("data.bin", "rb") as raw:
+        with wrap_file(raw, size) as reader:
+            data = reader.read()
+
+With :meth:`~rich.progress.Progress.wrap_file` you can instead pass ``task_id``, and the total is taken from that task when you do not pass ``total``. A task with no total raises ``ValueError``. This task option applies only to :meth:`~rich.progress.Progress.wrap_file`, not to the module-level :func:`~rich.progress.wrap_file`::
+
+    import os
+    from rich.progress import Progress
+
+    size = os.path.getsize("data.bin")
+    progress = Progress()
+    task_id = progress.add_task("Reading", total=size)
+    with progress:
+        with open("data.bin", "rb") as raw:
+            reader = progress.wrap_file(raw, task_id=task_id)
+            data = reader.read()
+
